  "notes": [
    "Supply / Demand / EMT / % price-reduced are point-in-time from the July 1 2026 deck (current-moment snapshot, 'Data Recorded As Of 7/1/2026').",
    "Sold figures cover MAY 2026 closings (deck slides titled 'MAY 2026 SOLD'). This deck lags sold data two months behind the deck date rather than the usual one month. S/L ratio is sale-to-last-list-price.",
    "Zillow HVI in this deck is the MAY 2026 index (slides titled 'May 2026 Home Prices'). M-o-M / Y-o-Y / 10-Yr columns are correctly labeled.",
    "Per-city comparison slides are titled 'Year-Over-Year Comparison'. The overview 'Y-O-Y CHANGES' column and per-city deltas are YEAR-OVER-YEAR and are stored in the legacy inventory_mom_pct / pending_mom_pct / emt_mom_days fields to preserve the pipeline; for THIS deck those legacy-named fields hold Y-o-Y values. expected_market_time_days_last_year is the 'Last Year: X Days' line from each per-city slide.",
    "GOTCHA — Dana Point ALL sold count: the per-city Dana Point sold slide reads 314 homes / $2.2m (count bleed corruption). The aggregate 'MAY 2026 SOLD All Homes' slide shows 31 homes / $2.1m, and $0-5M (29) + $5M+ (2) = 31. Using the aggregate slide: 31 / $2.1m / 95.6% / 8 days.",
    "GOTCHA — Newport Beach ALL sold count: the per-city Newport Beach sold slide reads 78 homes (Laguna Niguel's count bleeding in). The aggregate slide shows 63 homes, and $0-5M (44) + $5M+ (19) = 63. Using the aggregate slide: 63 / $3.7m / 98.2% / 26 days. ($5M+ median $7.2m from aggregate vs $7.1m per-city; used $7.2m.)",
    "GOTCHA — Irvine Zillow HVI: the North Coastal Area HVI slide shows Irvine -1.4% / -12.3% / +55.7% (a -12.3% Y-o-Y is implausible for a single month and inconsistent with the -0.8% Y-o-Y trend). The main HOME PRICE SNAPSHOT slide shows -0.1% / -1.2% / +55.7%. Using the main-snapshot values.",
    "GOTCHA — Newport Coast snapshot deltas: the North Coastal Area snapshot slide shows Newport Coast '+15% | -41 Days' which duplicates San Clemente's demand/EMT deltas. The overview slide and the per-city Newport Coast slide both show demand +33% (+2 pendings) and EMT -108 days (last year 280). Using +33% / -108.",
    "Minor rounding: several cities show a 1-day mismatch between the overview EMT delta and (current EMT - last-year EMT) from the per-city slide (e.g. Costa Mesa overview +24 vs slide 75-52=23; Newport Coast overview -108 vs slide 173-280=-107). Source rounding; overview delta stored in emt_mom_days, per-city 'Last Year' stored in expected_market_time_days_last_year.",
    "San Clemente is internally consistent: EMT 68, last year 109, delta -41 (109-41=68); inventory 122 (-29%, -49 homes, last year 171); demand 54 (+15%, +7 pendings, last year 47).",
    "OC-wide active price-reduction breakdown (Reports on Housing, 'Orange County - June 2026', as of 7/1/2026) captured under orange_county.reduction_breakdown.",
    "Median sale prices in this deck are rounded at source ($907k, $1.5m, $3.8m, etc.). Stored as the deck's rounded values.",
    "This deck has NO national/macro section (no mortgage-rate, NAR confidence, ARM, or Fannie forecast slides). All national.* fields are null this month."
